{"type":"message","id":"3c4cf1a1","parentId":"b8c9eb3a","timestamp":"2026-05-04T05:12:54.835Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The researcher agent failed to generate a response; maybe need fallback: try direct curl to RSS feeds. SOUL mentions: \"If researcher fails, try: curl -s 'https://decrypt.co/feed' or 'https://coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/'\". So we need to attempt fallback.\n\nPlan: If /tmp/research.json empty or contains error, run fallback: curl feed, maybe extract biggest news event using some simple processing? But we can't implement complex parsing. We can just fetch both feeds and pick first item maybe. But for pipeline, needs JSON with needed fields: topic_theme, combined_key_facts, primary_asset etc. Hard to produce.\n\nGiven limited ability, perhaps we can attempt to run researcher again with same command; maybe failure was transient. Could also try with --model? But maybe researcher agent is misconfigured. We could attempt again after short wait.\n\nLet's retry researcher once more. If still fails, we'll fallback to simple placeholder JSON with minimal required fields, but note that it's placeholder. However the rules say \"Never hallucinate URLs\". For JSON placeholder maybe okay.\n\nBut better try again.\n\nWe'll poll process to see if still running, but we already have a running command; we can kill it? There's process id session tender-tidepool. Could kill.\n\nWe'll use process(action=kill) for that session id.\n\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb9e45878d901168","name":"process","arguments":{"action":"kill","sessionId":"tender-tidepool"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"openai/gpt-oss-120b:free","usage":{"input":133,"output":308,"cacheRead":11920,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12361,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777871560738,"responseId":"gen-1777871561-uW