{"type":"message","id":"0f711aa3","parentId":"7354448f","timestamp":"2026-05-04T05:13:20.156Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The researcher agent failed to generate a response, probably needs fallback (curl RSS). The SOP says: \"If researcher fails, try: curl -s 'https://decrypt.co/feed' or 'https://coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/'\". So we need to fallback to manual fetch.\n\nWe can attempt to fetch RSS feeds and create a simple JSON ourselves? The requirement: need a Single-Topic JSON. Could be minimal with fields required later: topic_theme, combined_key_facts (array), primary_asset. We'll extract from RSS maybe.\n\nSimplify: fetch two feeds, pick first item, extract title, link, description. Then construct JSON with fields. Use web_fetch to get RSS and parse? web_fetch extracts markdown/text; not JSON. Could use curl and parse, but perhaps easier: just use curl to fetch feed, pick first entry, and construct JSON manually.\n\nWe can use exec to run curl and parse with grep/awk maybe.\n\nBut the pipeline expects later extraction of fields: topic_theme, combined_key_facts (first 2 items), primary_asset. We'll fabricate.\n\nLet's fetch Decrypt RSS: curl -s https://decrypt.co/feed. Then use simple extraction: maybe use grep \"<title>\" etc.\n\nSimplify: Use a small script to get title line and link.\n\nWe'll create a JSON like:\n{\n \"topic_theme\": \"Decryption of ...\",\n \"combined_key_facts\": [\"Fact 1\", \"Fact 2\"],\n \"primary_asset\": \"Bitcoin\"\n}\nWe can set primary_asset to \"Bitcoin\" as placeholder.\n\nOk.\n\nProceed: Use exec to fetch feed, extract first <title> after <item>. We'll write a small bash pipeline.\n\nCommand:\ncurl -s https://decrypt.co/feed | tr '\\n' ' ' | sed -n 's/.*<item>.*<title>\\([^<]*\\)<\\/title>.*<link>\\([^<]*\\)<\\/link>.*/\\1/p' \n\nBut might be complex. Simpler: Use xmlstarlet? Not installed.\n\nWe can just get first title after <item> using awk.\n\nLet's do:\ncurl -s https://decrypt.co/feed | awk '/<item>/,/<\\\\/item>/' | grep -m1 '<title>' | sed -e 's/.*<title>\\(.*\\)<\\\\/title>.*/\\1/'\n\nSimilarly link.\n\nWe'll then construct JSON with these.\n\nWe'll store to /tmp/research.json.\n\nProceed.\n\n<thinking>\nWe need to fallback: fetch Decrypt RSS, extract first item's title as topic_theme, take title and link as combined_key_facts (first two items), set primary_asset to \"Bitcoin\". Write JSON to /tmp/research.json.\n</thinking>","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-829e189036a65c65","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s https://decrypt.co/feed | awk '/<item>/,/<\\/item>/' | grep -m1 '<title>' | sed -e 's/.*<title>\\(.*\\)<\\/title>.*/\\1/'","wait":true}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"openai/gpt-oss-120b:free","usage":{"input":51,"output":638,"cacheRead":12048,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12737,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777871574872,"responseId":"gen-1777871575-O1CtniJ5IP3zKZb6mFXB"}}
{"type":"message","id":"9da7a880","parentId":"0f711aa3","timestamp":"2026-05-04T05:13:20.536Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-829e189036a65c65","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How Canton Network Lets Institutions Guard Against DeFi Security Risks: Digital Asset CEO"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":317,"aggregated":"How Canton Network Lets Institutions Guard Against DeFi Security Risks: Digital Asset CEO","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1777871600536}}
{"type":"message","id":"96836758","parentId":"9da7a880","timestamp":"2026-05-04T05:13:50.119Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Research agent failed to produce output. We need fallback as per SOUL: If researcher fails, try curl -s feeds. Could also try coindesk.\n\nWe need to create a JSON with required fields: topic_theme, combined_key_facts, primary_asset. The fallback we just got a title line; not enough.\n\nMaybe we should attempt to get a feed and parse multiple items to generate JSON manually? Could use simple approach: fetch both feeds and pick first item as biggest news. Use curl to get feed, pick first title/description.\n\nSimplify: fetch two RSS feeds, get first item's title, description; use that as topic_theme and combined_key_facts maybe. Primary asset could be extracted by checking for known asset names in title (Bitcoin, Ethereum, etc.) We'll just attempt simple heuristics.\n\nImplement: fetch decrypt feed title+description; fetch coindesk feed similar; combine.\n\nWe'll build JSON manually and write to /tmp/research.json.\n\nSteps:\n- fetch decrypt title and description via curl and xml parsing via grep/awk.\n- fetch coindesk title and description similarly.\n- Choose the longer description maybe? Or just pick decrypt as main.\n\nExtract primary asset: look for keywords Bitcoin, Ethereum, XRP, etc. Use case-insensitive grep.\n\nWe'll construct JSON: {\"topic_theme\":\"<title>\",\"combined_key_facts\":[\"<desc1>\",\"<desc2>\"],\"primary_asset\":\"<asset>\"}.\n\nLet's implement with shell commands.\n\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a369600f5489e65c","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Fetch Decrypt feed title and description\nDECRYPT_TITLE=$(curl -s https://decrypt.co/feed | grep -m1 '<title>' | sed -e 's/.*<title>\\(.*\\)<\\/title>.*/\\1/')\nDECRYPT_DESC=$(curl -s https://decrypt.co/feed | grep -A1 '<item>' | grep -m1 '<description>' | sed -e 's/.*<description>\\(.*\\)<\\/description>.*/\\1/')\n# Fetch CoinDesk feed title and description\nCOINDESK_TITLE=$(curl -s https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/ | grep -m1 '<title>' | sed -e 's/.*<title>\\(.*\\)<\\/title>.*/\\1/')\nCOINDESK_DESC=$(curl -s https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/ | grep -A1 '<item>' | grep -m1 '<description>' | sed -e 's/.*<description>\\(.*\\)<\\/description>.*/\\1/')\n# Determine primary asset\nPRIMARY=\"\"\nfor ASSET in Bitcoin Ethereum XRP Solana Cardano Polkadot \"Dogecoin\" \"Binance Coin\"; do\n  if echo \"$DECRYPT_TITLE $DECRYPT_DESC $COINDESK_TITLE $COINDESK_DESC\" | grep -i -q \"$ASSET\"; then\n    PRIMARY=$ASSET\n    break\n  fi\ndone\nif [ -z \"$PRIMARY\" ]; then PRIMARY=\"Crypto\"; fi\n# Build JSON\ncat > /tmp/research.json <<EOF\n{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"${DECRYPT_TITLE}\",\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\"${DECRYPT_DESC}\", \"${COINDESK_DESC}\"],\n  \"primary_asset\": \"${PRIMARY}\"\n}\nEOF","wait":true}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"openai/gpt-oss-120b:free","usage":{"input":100,"output":735,"cacheRead":12096,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12931,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777871600537,"responseId":"gen-1777871601-sEHv4z6SQjvtvqpOZX5V"}}
