{"type":"message","id":"e44c4048","parentId":"2abe4799","timestamp":"2026-05-04T05:14:27.878Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We had trouble using the researcher agent (maybe not configured). We fallback to manual fetch using curl to create a simple JSON with placeholders. The JSON currently has empty combined_key_facts; not ideal but we have something.\n\nWe need to proceed with writing article using writer agent. It expects RESEARCH_JSON. We'll pass the JSON content via environment variable or file path. The writer agent command expects reference to RESEARCH_JSON. In the original script, they use \"RESEARCH_JSON\" placeholder; maybe writer agent reads from that environment? I think they intend to literally embed the JSON content in the message, but we can substitute the file content.\n\nWe'll read the file content, then embed in the writer message with variable substitution.\n\nLet's read the research JSON content - we already have.\n\nNow step 2: run writer.\n\nWe'll remove writer sessions, then run openclaw agent writer with message referencing research JSON.\n\nMessage: \"First, read the COINOGRAPHY_TEMPLATE.md file in your workspace to learn your strict formatting rules. Then, write a 1100-1200 word crypto news article using these facts: {json}. You MUST finish the article completely, ending with the Sources and Word Count block.\"\n\nWe'll embed the JSON as inline (maybe use cat). We'll construct command with \"$(cat /tmp/research.json)\". Use Bash variable.\n\nWe also need to capture output to /tmp/crypto-article.md, then strip thinking blocks, check Word Count.\n\nWe'll exec the whole script steps sequentially.\n\nThen after article, we need to extract article title maybe first line starting with \"# \"?\n\nWe'll parse.\n\nNext, extract IMAGE_TOPIC and IMAGE_FACTS and IMAGE_ASSET from research JSON using jq.\n\nOur research JSON may have empty facts; but we proceed.\n\nWe'll then run creator agent.\n\nWe need to pass