{"type":"message","id":"3b53562e","parentId":"5fe17069","timestamp":"2026-05-04T05:16:18.577Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We have encountered failures: researcher agent didn't generate output, we resorted to crude curl approach producing limited info. Writer agent also fails to generate. Likely because openclaw agent commands require environment and maybe the system cannot spawn them; but we can still simulate? However instruction says we must actually execute commands, not hallucinate. If the agent fails, we should handle fallback: maybe retry with simpler messages or use other means.\n\nResearcher failure: maybe need to provide fallback feeds. SOUL says if researcher fails, try curl on feeds. We did that, generating simplistic JSON. That's okay.\n\nWriter failure: need fallback. Could we generate article ourselves via language model? But SOUL says we must delegate to writer agent. Yet writer agent failing could be because of missing COINOGRAPHY_TEMPLATE now provided. Maybe need to give writer more time? The exec may have completed quickly with no output, maybe writer agent didn't run due to missing credentials? We could attempt again with a simpler prompt, maybe not using $(cat ...) but passing the JSON inline.\n\nWe can embed the research JSON content in the message directly.\n\nLet's read /tmp/research.json content; we have it.\n\nWe'll construct a new writer command with explicit JSON string.\n\nWe also need to ensure that the writer agent tool is available. Let's attempt again.\n\nAlso may need to set environment variable for openclaw? Probably not.\n\nWe'll try:\n\nrm -f writer sessions, then openclaw agent --agent writer --message \"Here is the research JSON: { ... }. Write article per COINOGRAPHY_TEMPLATE.\"\n\nLet's prepare the JSON string from file but easy to embed via cat.\n\nWe'll run exec with command containing cat content inline via quoting.\n\nPotential quoting issues. Use single quotes around message and embed escaped JSON.\n\nWe'll do: MESSAGE=$(cat /tmp/research.json | tr -d '\\n' | sed \"s/\\\"/\\\\\\\"/g\") and then construct command.\n\nSimpler: use command substitution in bash: openclaw agent ... --message \"Research JSON: $(cat /tmp/research.json) ...\"\n\nLet's try.\n\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bff6f12d537f12b8","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"rm -f ~/.openclaw/agents/writer/sessions/sessions.json && openclaw agent --agent writer --message \"Research JSON: $(cat /tmp/research.json)\\nWrite a 1100-1200 word crypto news article following COINOGRAPHY_TEMPLATE.md rules. End with Sources and Word Count block.\" --deliver > /tmp/crypto-article.md","wait":true}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"openai/gpt-oss-120b:free","usage":{"input":71,"output":531,"cacheRead":13584,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":14186,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777871757605,"responseId":"gen-1777871758-GmgAuoMyb1agKHTkhIfc"}}
