{"type":"message","id":"2d7854d9","parentId":"4cd44901","timestamp":"2026-05-04T05:18:38.615Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-b5f621a5008b73d7","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I’m ready to create the feature image, but I need the article’s details to craft an appropriate scene.\n\nCould you please provide:\n\n- **Title** (the article’s headline)  \n- **Topic** (the general theme, e.g., regulation, price movement, DeFi hack, etc.)  \n- **Key facts** you’d like highlighted in the image  \n- **Crypto asset** (e.g., Bitcoin, Ethereum, Aave) that should appear visually  \n\nOnce I have those, I’ll build the prompt, run the Leonardo AI generation, and return the image file path.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1777871918615}}
{"type":"message","id":"b18555cc","parentId":"2d7854d9","timestamp":"2026-05-04T05:19:02.312Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The creator agent asks for details; we need to respond to it via session? Actually we are orchestrator; we can send a message to the creator session using sessions_send? The creator agent currently is an isolated session run via exec; we captured its output to a file. It is not interactive further. To provide details, we might need to re-run creator with message containing details. According to SOP, creator expects to generate image directly given the details. Since it asked, we need to give the details by re-invoking.\n\nSimplify: Instead of interactive, we can just run creator again with proper message including details. Provide details we extracted earlier: article title from article file, topic from research JSON, facts, asset.\n\nWe have variables exported in pipeline_vars.sh; we can source and then run creator again.\n\nWe'll construct a new message that includes the extracted variables.\n\nWe need to capture its output, which likely will be a file path. Let's run creator again.\n\n<thinking>\nWe need to run creator agent with message containing: Title, Topic, Key Facts, Asset.\n\nCommand:\nsource /tmp/pipeline_vars.sh && rm -f ~/.openclaw/agents/creator/sessions/sessions.json && openclaw agent --agent creator --message \"Generate a feature image for this article. Title: '$ARTICLE_TITLE'. Topic: $IMAGE_TOPIC. Key Facts: $IMAGE_FACTS. Crypto Asset: $IMAGE_ASSET. Use the Scene Formula in your SOUL.md to pick the right human subject and scene, then run the API calls and logo stamp steps exactly as defined in your SOUL.md.\" --deliver > /tmp/creator-output.txt\n\nWe'll execute.\n\nThen read /tmp/creator-output.txt; if it contains a file path ending with .jpg/.png we treat as success; else if contains IMAGE_FAILED we handle fallback.\n\nProceed.\n\n</thinking>","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type"